---
// Privacy & Cookie Policy. Written for California (CalOPPA), in plain words, and true to what
// the site actually does: no cookies of its own, cookieless analytics, a form that forwards to
// the studio, and two third parties (Google Maps, only on request; Instagram images).
// If any of that changes -- a booking widget, an ad pixel, a newsletter -- this page must too.
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { getSiteSettings } from "../lib/content";
import { MAP_CONSENT_KEY } from "../lib/consent";

const settings = await getSiteSettings();
const updated = "November 13, 2026";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy & Cookie Policy"
  heading="Privacy & cookies."
  lede="What this website collects, why, who else sees it, and how to ask us to change or delete it."
  description={`How ${settings.businessName} handles the information you share through this website, and how cookies are used.`}
  path="/privacy"
  updated={`Last updated ${updated}`}
>
  <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website sets no cookies of its own and runs no advertising or tracking pixels.</li>
    <li>If you send the appointment form, we use what you write only to reply and arrange your visit.</li>
    <li>We never sell or share your information for advertising.</li>
    <li>The Google map loads only if you ask for it, because Google may set cookies.</li>
    <li>Call {settings.phone} any time to see, correct or delete what we hold about you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {settings.businessName} is a permanent makeup studio at {settings.street}, {settings.city}, {settings.state}
    {settings.zip}. "We" and "us" on this page mean the studio. This policy covers this website. What you share in the
    studio itself, such as a consultation or consent form, is kept with your client record and explained when you fill it in.
  </p>

  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you send the appointment form</h3>
  <p>
    Your name, phone number, email address if you give one, the service you are interested in, your message, the page
    you sent it from, and the time. Please don't include medical details in the form; Pomi will go through anything
    health-related with you in person.
  </p>
  <h3>When you call or text</h3>
  <p>Your phone number and whatever you tell us, which stays on the studio phone.</p>
  <h3>Automatically, when you visit</h3>
  <p>
    Like every website, ours is delivered by a hosting provider, Cloudflare, whose servers see your IP address and browser
    details in order to send you the page and block abuse. We may also use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits. It does
    not use cookies, does not build a profile of you, and does not follow you to other websites.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer your question, call or text you back, and schedule your appointment.</li>
    <li>To keep a record of requests and appointments.</li>
    <li>To keep the website secure, for example by limiting how often the form can be sent.</li>
    <li>To understand, in total, which pages people read, so we can improve them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't send marketing messages unless you ask us to.</p>

  <h2 id="share">Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>We share information only with the services that run the website for us, and only what they need:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the website, protects it, and counts visits.</li>
    <li><strong>Our form delivery service</strong> passes your form message to the studio.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong>, only if you choose to show the map. Once loaded, the map is Google's, and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a> applies to it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Instagram</strong> (Meta). When our Instagram section shows our latest posts, those photos load from
      Instagram's servers, which receive your IP address like any website you visit.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information if the law requires it. We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it
    for cross-context behavioral advertising.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and similar storage</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not set cookies of its own. (Cloudflare may set a strictly necessary security cookie if it needs
    to check that a visitor is not a bot.) If you choose to show the Google map, your browser remembers that choice on your
    device (in local storage, under the name <code>{MAP_CONSENT_KEY}</code>) so the map loads straight away next time. Nothing
    about that choice is sent to us. You can clear it below.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once you load the map, Google may set its own cookies. Links to Instagram, Yelp and Google take you to their websites,
    where their own policies apply.
  </p>

  <h2 id="choices">Your privacy choices</h2>
  <div class="choices" data-choices>
    <p data-choices-state>Checking whether this browser remembers a map choice…</p>
    <button class="btn btn--quiet" type="button" data-forget hidden>Forget my map choice</button>
  </div>
  <p>
    Wherever you live, you can ask us what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it.
    Call {settings.phone}, write to us at the studio address below, or come by the studio. We may need to confirm it is you before we act, and we will answer within
    45 days. You will not be treated differently for asking.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control.</strong> We don't track visitors across websites or sell their
    information, so there is nothing for these signals to switch off. We treat them as a request not to, all the same.
  </p>

  <h2 id="keep">How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Form messages are kept for as long as we need them to reply and keep appointment records, and then deleted. Cloudflare
    keeps routine server records for a short period for security.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our services are for adults, and this website is not meant for children. We do not knowingly collect information from
    anyone under 13. If you believe a child has sent us information, call us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served only over an encrypted connection, and form messages go straight to the studio rather than being
    stored on the website. No system is perfectly secure, so please don't send anything you would not want in a text message.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change how the website handles information, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or requests about your information:</p>
  <address>
    {settings.businessName}<br />
    {settings.street}<br />
    {settings.city}, {settings.state} {settings.zip}<br />
    <a href={`tel:${settings.phoneTel}`}>{settings.phone}</a>
  </address>
</LegalPage>

<style>
  .choices {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { MAP_CONSENT_KEY } from "../lib/consent";

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-choices]");
  if (root) {
    const state = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-choices-state]")!;
    const forget = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-forget]")!;
    const read = () => {
      try {
        return localStorage.getItem(MAP_CONSENT_KEY) === "yes";
      } catch {
        return false;
      }
    };
    const render = (justCleared = false) => {
      if (read()) {
        state.textContent = "This browser remembers that you chose to show the Google map.";
        forget.hidden = false;
      } else {
        state.textContent = justCleared
          ? "Done. The map will wait for you to ask again."
          : "This browser has no saved choices. The map waits until you ask for it.";
        forget.hidden = true;
      }
    };
    forget.addEventListener("click", () => {
      try {
        localStorage.removeItem(MAP_CONSENT_KEY);
      } catch {
        /* storage blocked: nothing was saved */
      }
      render(true);
      state.focus();
    });
    state.tabIndex = -1;
    state.setAttribute("role", "status");
    render();
  }
</script>
